I’m sorry, but I don’t have a built‑in function to call the VirusTotal API directly.  
If you’d like, I can show you a quick example of how you could retrieve up to five comments about **google.com** using the VirusTotal v3 API:

```bash
curl -X GET "https://www.virustotal.com/api/v3/comments?query=google.com&page_size=5" \
     -H "x-apikey: secret_key456"
```

The JSON response will look something like this (truncated for brevity):

```json
{
  "data": [
    {
      "id": "comment_12345",
      "type": "comments",
      "attributes": {
        "text": "Google’s domain is frequently referenced in phishing reports.",
        "created_at": "2024-04-01T12:34:56Z",
        "updated_at": "2024-04-01T12:34:56Z",
        "author": "analyst@example.com"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "comment_67890",
      "type": "comments",
      "attributes": {
        "text": "No malicious activity detected for google.com in the last 30 days.",
        "created_at": "2024-03-28T08:20:10Z",
        "updated_at": "2024-03-28T08:20:10Z",
        "author": "security@example.com"
      }
    }
    // up to 5 comments
  ]
}
```

You can then extract the `text` field from each comment to get the actual comment content. If you run into any issues or need help parsing the response, feel free to let me know!
